10810c66129c14dc.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/7e/7e1a0c5dd2b4aadf7efe78d903234b8d00cf4fa92eb7a3b41209a856f2d14b01.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.25$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/a9/a90d7306e3f88a31609e368f9362248d6a12b7922b6a9e8c9f980ab31e7fb140.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." 13194139537076 17592186576411 false] [17592186403647 1074 "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/21/215dd0c920e700a75896fc54751ec20d197487a2c992cd8910810c66129c14dc.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/7e/7e1a0c5dd2b4aadf7efe78d903234b8d00cf4fa92eb7a3b41209a856f2d14b01.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.25$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/a9/a90d7306e3f88a31609e368f9362248d6a12b7922b6a9e8c9f980ab31e7fb140.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement “It's neither a type I nor a type II region” is true." 13194139537076 17592186576411 true] [17592186403787 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=-1 \\\\ 2x-4y &=3 \\\\ x+y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537076 17592186576411 true] [17592186403787 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=-1 \\\\ 2x-4y &=3 \\\\ x+y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n\n- **II.** The system has a unique solution\n\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent" 13194139537076 17592186576411 false] [17592186403787 1074 "To classify the system, we will first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=\\frac{9}{2},$ and it has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." 13194139537076 17592186576411 false] [17592186403787 1074 "To classify the system, we will first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=\\frac{9}{2},$ and it has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is inconsistent” is true." 13194139537076 17592186576411 true] [17592186403864 1071 "Which of the following equations has no solutions for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}?$\n\nI. $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=0$ $$\nII. $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=8$\nIII. $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{7}{3}$\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537076 17592186576411 false] [17592186403864 1071 "Which of the following equations has no solutions for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537076 17592186576411 true] [17592186403864 1074 "Recall that the range of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=0$ has no solutions." 13194139537076 17592186576411 true] [17592186403864 1074 "Recall that the range of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation I has no solutions." 13194139537076 17592186576411 false] [17592186403905 1071 "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n\nI. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2}$\nII. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=12$\nIII. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{7}$\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537076 17592186576411 false] [17592186403905 1071 "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537076 17592186576411 true] [17592186403905 1074 "Recall that the range of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup 