nd the statement is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent \"$9$ is divisible by $5$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139537076 17592186576411 false] [17592186406949 1074 "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement “**If** $12$ is divisible by $3$, **then** $9$ is divisible by $4.$” is false. The antecedent \"$12$ is divisible by $3$\" is true, and the consequent \"$9$ is divisible by $4$\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement “**If** $5$ is divisible by $2$, **then** $10$ is divisible by $5.$” is true. The antecedent \"$5$ is divisible by $2$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement “**If** $9$ is divisible by $5$, **then** $6$ is divisible by $3.$” is true. Again, the antecedent \"$9$ is divisible by $5$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “**If** $5$ is divisible by $2$, **then** $10$ is divisible by $5.$”; “**If** $9$ is divisible by $5$, **then** $6$ is divisible by $3.$” only." 13194139537076 17592186576411 true] [17592186406950 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537076 17592186576411 true] [17592186406950 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** **If** $7$ is an even number, **then** $6$ is an odd number.\n- **II.** **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an even number.\n- **III.** **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an odd number." 13194139537076 17592186576411 false] [17592186406950 1074 "An 